title: <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> Party Conference
subtitle: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> chooses their new central committee - will the Gembirth Affair have an influence on their choice?
new-page: true
view-if: collectivist_relation >= 50 and wittorf_soviet_union = 1 and year = 1929 and month >= 6 and month <= 8
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: collectivist_party_conference_seen = 1
tags: event

= <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> Party Conference

Now is the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s national party conference, where they will choose their new leadership. The shadow of the Gembirth Affair hangs over it. On one hand are the hardline supporters of Halsmark, who support a "<span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntists</span>" policy that places the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> as equivalent to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>. On the other hand is the "Conciliator" faction, who support a more cooperative policy towards the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>.

After our discussion with the <span style="color: #940000;">Central Unions</span>, we are inclined to believe that <span style="color: #8B0000;">Halsmark</span> is at least open to the Conciliators. In order to affect the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s leadership elections, we have to influence both the <span style="color: #D50000;">Comintern</span> leaders as as well as the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> membership.

- @conciliator_success
- @conciliator_fail


@conciliator_success
title: The Conciliators are the new leadership of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
choose-if: (levi_advisor or rosenfeld_advisor) and (left_strength >= reformist_strength) and (collectivist_relation >= 50) 
unavailable-subtitle: [?  if not levi_advisor and not rosenfeld_advisor: Our party leadership is not left-wing enough. ?] [? if left_strength < reformist_strength: The <span style="color: #D50000;">Comintern</span> doubts our commitment to <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformism</span>. ?]
on-arrival: collectivist_leader = "Conciliators"; communist_coalition += 3; collectivist_relation += 10*(1-dissent); left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 8; pro_republic += (collectivist_votes / 2)
achievement: versohnler

With our support, the Conciliators have won the leadership contest! The new leadership is a group of Conciliators, including Eamon Ewlan, Kelby Steunenberg, and Joren Merrow. Halsmark remains, but largely as a figurehead only, it seems. We hope that the new leadership will be more inclined towards cooperation.


@conciliator_fail
title: Halsmark retains his leadership position.

Unfortunately, we could not influence the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> leadership election against the hardliners. Halsmark quickly moves to consolidate absolute leadership, expelling or exiling his opponents.
